## L5 — `_charge_ingest` per-model attribution can price a shared provider id at the wrong surface rate

- **Status:** not started — low priority
- **Where:** `pipeline/pipeline/ingest/worker.py:393-426` (`spec = vision if
  model_id == vision.provider_model_id else ingest`)

### Problem

Token attribution picks the rate card by comparing `provider_model_id` strings. If the
ingest and vision pins ever resolve to the same provider model id, all its tokens are
priced at the vision surface's rate. Today the two surfaces use distinct models, so this
is latent; fixing it properly means threading the surface through
`obs.record_completion` (which currently records only provider+model), i.e. touching
every model call site. Recommend deferring until surfaces can actually share a model.

